<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnundātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		inundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an overflowing</i>, <i>inundating</i>, <i>inundation</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluminum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 11, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coërcere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inundationes Tiberis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Oth. 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nili,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Pan. 30 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 3, 42</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrarum,</span>”
				<i>the deluge</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 13, 14, § 69</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sol. 34, 1</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of a crowd of people, Schol. <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
			249</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Of horses: inundatione equorum ejus operiet te
					pulvis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Ezech. 26, 10</span></i>
			.—Of troubles, sorrow, <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Job, 21, 17</span></i>.</div>
